Z||000008||skitime||10-22-2001||11:19 AM||||   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>hey skitime, what did you do to put those fog/driving lights in?  That looks really good, I think your car is definitely top 5 fieros I ever seen.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Thanks for the compliments.  The lights were ordered to fit the exact size of the opening. The driving lights are mounted using the U-shaped brackets that came with the lights. The mounts are bolted to the bottom of the original nose using some reinforcement. The opening itself adds to the support of the light since it fits in snuggly into the opening.   My light pockets are smaller than Lawrences because I used rear reflector pockets from a back bumper of a GT and Lawrence used the front turn signal pockets from a GT nose.<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/P000821-1.jpg">   <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 10-22-2001).]||||reg||7
