Z||000011||MinnGreenGT||10-22-2001||05:07 PM||||Mr.Stang... the blue/silver choptop v8 you refer to is known as the "purple pavement eater" and can be found on <A HREF="http://www.v8archie.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.v8archie.com</A>  (I believe in the "for sale" section). It is an awsome ride!<P>Skitime- and I was just going to ask how you did the recess for the light... nevermind!||||reg||1
Z||000012||MinnGreenGT||10-22-2001||05:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Spektrum-87GT:<BR><B>...was a notchback 85 gt   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Technically the PPE wasn't an '85 Notchback. Check out the taillights- Fastback GT models... the sail panel was custom formed to resemble a notchback, but retain the fastback lights & decklid. Mmmm... yummy.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/warber13sm.jpg"> <BR>pic copyright v8archie...used without permission  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
